UPSTREAM SOURCES

  Land Use Generalised, 2015 to 2025 (one layer a year, from the valuation land use codes and the valuation cadastre on
  30 June each year), Department for Housing and Urban Development, Government of South Australia. Data.SA: the
  catalogue lists it under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0); the files carry a licence note for Creative
  Commons Attribution 3.0 Australia (CC BY 3.0 AU). Both allow republishing with attribution.
  https://data.sa.gov.au/data/dataset/land-use-generalised
    Changes: the 2018 and 2025 layers cut to Greater Adelaide and laid over each other; classes named in words;
    slivers under 500 m2 or thinner than 3 m left out; the area of each class summed each year.

  Land Division Applications, Department for Housing and Urban Development, Government of South Australia. Data.SA:
  CC BY 4.0 on the catalogue, CC BY 3.0 AU on the files. https://data.sa.gov.au/data/dataset/land-division-applications
    Changes: the allotments for homes (purpose RES or CRES) of applications lodged 1 July 2018 to 30 June 2025 and
    approved (under the Development Act 1993 or the Planning, Development and Infrastructure Act 2016), each placed by
    its inside point; withdrawn, refused, lapsed, cancelled and superseded ones left out.

  Australian Bureau of Statistics, Australian Statistical Geography Standard (ASGS) Edition 3: Statistical Areas
  Level 2, Local Government Areas and Greater Capital City Statistical Areas, 2021. Based on ABS data, licensed under
  CC BY 4.0. Simplified and converted by Plotlay.

  Base map in the Plotlay project and the app screenshots: Plotlay Quiet, made from OpenStreetMap data
  (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database License (ODbL). It is a picture behind the data only: no data in this
  repository is taken from OpenStreetMap.

POWER BI MAP CONTEXT
  The Shape Map in powerbi/ draws South Australia's local government areas round the SA2s: ABS ASGS Edition 3 (2021),
  CC BY 4.0, simplified. The sea is the map background where no land is drawn.

NOT INCLUDED
  The state-wide land use layers themselves (about 1 GB for the eleven years) are not copied here: python/download.py
  fetches them from Data.SA. Nothing in data/ is derived from OpenStreetMap, and no imagery was traced. Nothing here
  implies endorsement by the Department for Housing and Urban Development or the ABS.

